# Chess Dad configuration. Copy to `.env.local` and adjust.

# --- Engine ---
# Path to the Stockfish binary (default: resolve `stockfish` on PATH).
STOCKFISH_PATH=stockfish
# Default analysis depth for game review (14 = fast, 18 = deep).
ANALYSIS_DEPTH=14
ENGINE_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
# Per-engine UCI options. Lower threads when running many workers.
ENGINE_THREADS=2
ENGINE_HASH_MB=64
# Stockfish process pool size (one engine per concurrent game).
# ENGINE_POOL_SIZE=5

# --- Analysis queue (the MQ) + worker pool ---
# How many games are analysed at once. Defaults to min(4, cpus - 1).
# WORKER_CONCURRENCY=4
# How often an idle worker polls the queue (ms).
# WORKER_POLL_MS=750
# Job lease before an unfinished job is reclaimed (ms).
# JOB_LEASE_MS=120000
# Attempts per job before it is marked failed.
# JOB_MAX_ATTEMPTS=2
# How many analysis jobs may wait at once. Past this, an import or a bulk
# analysis turns the extra games away and says so, instead of accepting work that
# will not run for hours. Backpressure, not a hard limit on the library.
# MAX_QUEUE_DEPTH=200

# --- Import ---
MAX_GAMES_PER_SOURCE=100
# Optional: a Lichess OAuth token (personal API access token) raises rate limits
# and can fetch private games. Public games work without it.
LICHESS_TOKEN=

# --- AI coaching (per profile, configured in the browser) ---
#
# There is deliberately no provider, model or API key here any more. Each profile
# adds its own providers on the Profiles screen — OpenAI, Anthropic, Google,
# DeepSeek, a local Ollama, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint — and the key is
# stored in that browser, passed to the server only inside the one AI request
# that uses it, and never written down. The default analysis is the free,
# deterministic Stockfish-grounded coach, which needs no key at all; AI is only
# used when a user explicitly re-analyses a move or a game.
#
# Two server-side limits remain. A single provider call is capped by
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS — 120s by default, because a reasoning model can legitimately
# think for that long, and a connection can override it per provider on the
# Profiles screen. A whole request (one move, or every flagged move in a game) is
# capped by LLM_BATCH_BUDGET_MS; once it is spent the route stops starting new
# calls and returns the readings it already has instead of being killed mid-game.
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# LLM_BATCH_BUDGET_MS=540000
#
# Note that reasoning/thinking modes are OFF per connection by default: reasoning
# tokens are billed as output and can run for minutes. One measured DeepSeek call
# returned 24,699 reasoning tokens over 119 seconds, past the timeout above, so
# the answer was paid for and thrown away. A connection can opt in explicitly.

# --- Storage (local-first) ---
# CHESSDAD_DB_PATH=./data/chessdad.db
